# Power Demand Forecasting Using Machine Learning


Power demand forecasting is a critical task in the energy sector, enabling utility providers and grid operators to efficiently manage electricity generation, distribution, and consumption. Accurate forecasting helps reduce operational costs, improve resource allocation, prevent power shortages, and support sustainable energy planning.

This project presents an end-to-end machine learning solution for forecasting hourly power demand using historical electricity consumption data. The workflow begins with data ingestion and preprocessing, where missing values, duplicate records, and inconsistencies are handled to ensure data quality.

Feature engineering techniques are applied to extract valuable temporal information from the timestamp data, including hour, day, week, month, quarter, year, weekend indicators, and holiday-related features. These engineered features help machine learning models capture seasonal trends, daily usage patterns, and long-term demand fluctuations.

The project includes comprehensive Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) to uncover trends, seasonality, and anomalies in electricity consumption. Various visualizations are used to understand demand behavior across different time periods.

Multiple machine learning algorithms are implemented and evaluated, including:


* Random Forest Regressor
* XGBoost Regressor
* LightGBM Regressor


Each model is trained and tested using historical power demand data, and performance is assessed using industry-standard evaluation metrics such as:

* Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
* Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
* Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE)
* R² Score

The system compares model performance and identifies the most accurate forecasting approach. Forecast results are visualized through interactive charts that allow users to compare actual versus predicted demand values.

To improve usability, the project includes a Streamlit-based web application where users can upload their own datasets, train forecasting models, visualize trends, compare model performance, and generate future power demand predictions through an intuitive interface.

### Project Objectives

* Forecast future electricity demand with high accuracy.
* Compare multiple machine learning algorithms.
* Build a reusable and scalable forecasting pipeline.
* Provide interactive visualization and reporting.
* Enable users to perform forecasting through a user-friendly web application.

### Business Impact

Accurate power demand forecasting helps organizations:

* Optimize power generation schedules.
* Reduce energy wastage and operational costs.
* Improve grid stability and reliability.
* Support demand-side management strategies.
* Enhance long-term energy planning and decision-making.

This project demonstrates practical applications of data science, machine learning, time series analysis, feature engineering, and interactive dashboard development in solving real-world energy forecasting challenges.
